Narrator: Pick the language Vexa greets in. It switches the moment your caller does.

203
00:15:41,439 --> 00:15:46,795
Narrator: Callers in India mix languages, type them in English letters, and count in lakhs.

204
00:15:46,795 --> 00:15:52,548
Narrator: Vexa now understands all of that: dates like kal and parso, numbers like dedh lakh, yes

205
00:15:52,548 --> 00:15:55,524
Narrator: and no in every language, and Indian English.

206
00:15:55,524 --> 00:16:00,020
Narrator: And a quick haan or hmm while Vexa is talking no longer cuts it off.

207
00:16:03,570 --> 00:16:09,386
Narrator: We measured it. On one hundred and fifty seven test sentences, Vexa without the model went

208
00:16:09,386 --> 00:16:15,397
Narrator: from fifteen percent to ninety nine. With Claude, from eighty to one hundred percent, and the

209
00:16:15,397 --> 00:16:18,434
Narrator: same on fifty new phrasings we never tuned for.

210
00:16:18,434 --> 00:16:23,281
Narrator: Next: Indian speech engines, measured on real voices over real phone lines.

211
00:16:26,831 --> 00:16:32,505
Narrator: How it works. Claude understands what the caller says, in any of the eight languages.

212
00:16:32,505 --> 00:16:38,313
Narrator: A flow engine then decides exactly what to ask next, when to confirm, when to transfer,

213
00:16:38,313 --> 00:16:42,719
Narrator: and when to hang up. That keeps calls predictable, fast and cheap.

214
00:16:44,469 --> 00:16:47,428
Narrator: Flows are playbooks for each kind of call:

215
00:16:47,428 --> 00:16:55,390
Narrator: deliveries, bank offers, family, bookings, directions, stock. You can see how many questions Vexa skipped because

216
00:16:55,390 --> 00:16:57,504
Narrator: callers already answered them.

217
00:16:59,654 --> 00:17:03,036
Narrator: Every step can be edited from your phone:

218
00:17:03,036 --> 00:17:06,171
Narrator: ask, confirm, branch, act or transfer.

219
00:17:08,321 --> 00:17:13,908
Narrator: Activity shows every call with its summary, the flow it followed, and what needs your follow-up.

220
00:17:16,058 --> 00:17:21,862
Narrator: Each call shows the facts Vexa captured, the actions it took, a ready to send reply,

221
00:17:21,862 --> 00:17:23,382
Narrator: and the exact AI cost.

222
00:17:25,632 --> 00:17:34,594
Narrator: Finally, what it cost. All 14 calls, plus the two extra requests, used 138,467 tokens on

223
00:17:34,594 --> 00:17:39,381
Narrator: Claude Opus 5.5, for a total of about 74 cents.

224
00:17:39,381 --> 00:17:45,187
Narrator: That is roughly 5.2 cents per call, or about 4.34 rupees.

225
00:17:45,637 --> 00:17:51,050
Narrator: A multilingual call costs a little more, because Vexa also translates its replies.

226
00:17:55,100 --> 00:18:00,890
Narrator: What is next: Indian speech engines and Indian voices, then a real Indian phone number with

227
00:18:00,890 --> 00:18:06,362
Narrator: replies inside one and a half seconds, then the Android app with WhatsApp and UPI, and

228
00:18:06,362 --> 00:18:07,316
Narrator: business tools.

229
00:18:07,766 --> 00:18:14,027
Narrator: Vexa: every call answered, in your caller’s language, and you are only interrupted when it matters.
